摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A drop-in replacement for Claude Code's Monitor tool, built for DeepSeek Harness.","id":"gh:1333440937","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-monitor","slug":"AbnerAI/dsh-monitor","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A drop-in replacement for Claude Code's Monitor tool, built for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-monitor"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**A drop-in replacement for Claude Code's `Monitor` tool, built for DeepSeek Harness.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"`dsh-monitor` is a harness plugin that arms **persistent, background watchers** on message sources. "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"When new content arrives, the plugin **wakes the owning agent** — delivering a plugin-sourced user m"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"essage into the session, exactly like Claude Code's `<task-notification>` mechanism."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"If you rely on Claude Code's Monitor to stay responsive to inbound messages while a shell is idle, t"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"his plugin gives you the same capability inside DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"The model calls the `monitor` tool to arm a watcher on a source:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"- **`source: file`** — an append-only NDJSON inbox. New lines are delivered as they land.\n- **`sourc"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"e: command`** — a shell command re-run on an interval. Its output delta since the last run is delive"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ommand`** — a shell command re-run on an interval. Its output delta since the last run is delivered."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"On each new message the plugin wakes the agent:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Agent state | Behavior |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| **idle** | `agent.followup()` — opens a new turn (harness analog of Claude Code's `<task-notificat"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ion>`) |\n| **busy** | `agent.inject()` — queues the message into the next step |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Watchers are durable within the session, disarmable on demand, and torn down automatically when the "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"e within the session, disarmable on demand, and torn down automatically when the plugin is unloaded."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"> `dsh plugin --profile <name> <args...>` is a thin pnpm forwarder: it runs\n> `pnpm <args...>` in th"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"e profile directory, then adds any installed package\n> that declares `dsh.bundle` to the profile's l"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ayer stack automatically."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### From npm"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### From git"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### From a local directory"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"> When installing a local directory, run `pnpm install` inside the package\n> first — `link:` install"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"s do not resolve the package's own dependencies\n> automatically."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Manual alternative: add `dsh-monitor` to the profile's `dsh.profile.bundles`\nand include this packag"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"e's `cordis.patch.yml` via its `dsh.bundle.patch`\ndeclaration."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Tell the agent to arm a watcher on an inbox file:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- `path` must be an **absolute path** (or start with `~` — the plugin expands it). Node's `fs` does "},{"id":"p26s2","text":"not expand `~` itself.\n- `poll_interval_ms` defaults to 2000; 1000 is a good balance for chat-like i"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"and `~` itself.\n- `poll_interval_ms` defaults to 2000; 1000 is a good balance for chat-like inboxes."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The tool returns a watcher id, e.g. `monitor-1`. From then on, every new line written to the file wa"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"kes the agent automatically."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Manage watchers at any time:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"To watch a command's changing output instead of a file:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### `monitor`"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Arm a persistent watcher."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"| `source` | `\"file\" \\| \"command\"` | yes | `file` = watch an append-only NDJSON inbox; `command` = p"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"oll a shell command's output |\n| `path` | string | for `file` | path of the NDJSON inbox (absolute, "},{"id":"p36s3","text":"or `~`-prefixed) |\n| `command` | string | for `command` | shell command to poll |\n| `cwd` | string |"},{"id":"p36s4","text":" no | working directory for the command (defaults to the process cwd) |\n| `poll_interval_ms` | numbe"},{"id":"p36s5","text":"r | no | poll interval in ms (default 2000) |\n| `name` | string | no | short label used in wake-up m"},{"id":"p36s6","text":"essages and `monitor_list` |"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Returns a watcher id. Each new NDJSON line (or command-output delta) is delivered as a plugin-source"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"d notice that wakes the agent."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"> **Implementation note.** Polling uses plain global `setInterval` with cleanup registered via `ctx."},{"id":"p38s2","text":"effect` — the same timer convention as `dsh-schedule`. The Cordis timer-service mixin (`ctx.setInter"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"val`) is intentionally **not** used: it is only resolvable from the host context, not from tool-exec"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"ution contexts, and calling it throws `cannot get property \"timer\" without inject`."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"### `monitor_list`"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"List armed watchers with their ids, sources, and delivery counts. Empty output means nothing is arme"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"st armed watchers with their ids, sources, and delivery counts. Empty output means nothing is armed."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"### `monitor_stop`"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Disarm a watcher by id. Returns whether it was still armed."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## NDJSON inbox format"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Each line is a JSON object; the `content` field is delivered if present, otherwise the raw line:"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"Any append-only NDJSON file works. The format pairs naturally with messaging and notification broker"},{"id":"p46s2","text":"s: a broker appends one record per inbound message, and a watcher on the file wakes the agent as new"},{"id":"p46s3","text":" records land. This mirrors the contract Claude Code Monitor exposes for its own inbox watchers."},{"id":"p47s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) with a Cordis-based plugin loader (bundles / `cordis.patch.yml`).\n- Peer de"},{"id":"p48s2","text":"pendencies: `dsh-agent`, `dsh-llm`, `dsh-tools`, `cordis` (satisfied by the harness runtime)."},{"id":"p49s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
